{"id": "glm2_run_length_decode", "signature": "solve(s)", "statement": "Given a string s that is a run-length encoding — each maximal run of a repeated character is written as the character followed by its count, with the count omitted entirely when the run has length 1 — return the decoded string. Counts are single digits between 1 and 9. The empty string decodes to the empty string.", "tests": [{"args": [""], "expected": ""}, {"args": ["a3"], "expected": "aaa"}, {"args": ["a1b"], "expected": "ab"}, {"args": ["ab3c2"], "expected": "abbbcc"}, {"args": ["z9"], "expected": "zzzzzzzzz"}, {"args": ["x1y1z1"], "expected": "xyz"}, {"args": ["q5w"], "expected": "qqqqqw"}, {"args": ["m1"], "expected": "m"}, {"args": ["a2b2c2"], "expected": "aabbcc"}, {"args": ["p"], "expected": "p"}, {"args": ["a9b1"], "expected": "aaaaaaaaab"}, {"args": ["w1x2"], "expected": "wxx"}], "facts": [["arg", "s", "string"], ["iterate", "s"], ["ask", "run_length"], ["run_output", "decoded"]], "deps": {"schema": ["run_encode"], "uses": ["run_length_decode"], "solution_sha256": "d4a600d08beb95fe3ee68074f6cdd7705497de104e1aa1e6c98447377775b899", "reference_sha256": "2529afe70adf7ab546b4223fe8c0b0a0e5c45c573bc79a97d693305964f934b3"}}